    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d649">

                <pb facs="0688" n="590" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg590"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.113/1402: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul at Saigon
                        (Waterman)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-10-26T19:00:00-05:00">October 26, 1932—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your despatch of August 8 concerning transit of goods through Indo-China.</p>
                <p>In the absence of a specific case, Department feels that it would be inopportune
                    to raise this question at least until commercial treaty negotiations with
                        France<anchor n="22" xml:id="d649-f1"/> have been concluded. Please report
                    fully with regard to French regulations and practices in respect of this transit
                    trade.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
